VoxType on Omaxian OS
=====================
1. Press Super+Ctrl+V. The first time, a terminal opens and asks you to pick
   a speech model (`voxtype setup model`, needs internet; base.en ~142 MB,
   tiny.en ~75 MB). No model is shipped on the ISO.
2. Press Super+Ctrl+V to start recording, again to stop: the text is put on
   the X11 clipboard (xclip). Paste it with Ctrl+V (Shift+Insert / middle
   click in terminals).
The daemon runs per user, started on demand (no systemd, so the upstream
systemd user unit is unused), with its evdev hotkey off (--no-hotkey): i3
owns the key. For typing at the cursor instead of the clipboard, Omaxian
ships ydotool (omaxian-ydotool; ydotoold is started by i3 and your user is
in the "input" group): set [output] mode in ~/.config/voxtype/config.toml.
Disable the keybinding: delete ~/.config/i3/config.d/60-voxtype.conf.
